amples de guitarras metálicas) y KMFDM. Chicago la completa: Ministry de Al Jourgensen (The Land Of Rape And Honey, «Jesus Built My Hot Rod»), Revolting Cocks, Pigface de Martin Atkins y, de ahí, Nine Inch Nails de Trent Reznor, que cambia el destino del industrial (Pretty Hate Machine, The Downward Spiral). El post-industrial: Neurosis, Steel Pole Bath Tub, Cop Shoot Cop, Missing Foundation, Pain Teens, Godflesh de Justin Broadrick, y los proyectos de Jello Biafra (Lard, Tumor Circus).","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Gótico e industrial","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial-metal"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":56045184465986,"artist":"KMFDM","artist_id":249511102701788,"title":"What Do You Know Deutschland","year":1986,"ess":0,"yt":"b0tCv7sNcF4","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Metal industrial y post-industrial","scene_id":225164069558548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial-metal","chapters":["Sección 5.22"],"pages":[[1,210,null]]},{"id":204594879857940,"artist":"KMFDM","artist_id":249511102701788,"title":"Naive","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"8Dzs4TS_rKc","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Metal industrial y post-industrial","scene_id":225164069558548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial-metal","chapters":["Sección 5.22"],"pages":[[1,210,null]]},{"id":144470462600027,"artist":"KMFDM","artist_id":249511102701788,"title":"Angst","year":1993,"ess":0,"yt":"Gp-z0QJefIY","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Metal industrial y post-industrial","scene_id":225164069558548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial-metal","chapters":["Sección 5.22"],"pages":[[1,210,null]]},{"id":68987195169663,"artist":"KMFDM","artist_id":249511102701788,"title":"Nihil","year":1995,"ess":0,"yt":"p511mTLz2qU","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Metal industrial y post-industrial","scene_id":225164069558548,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#industrial-metal","chapters":["Sección 5.22"],"pages":[[1,210,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":255,"text":"…music became a mass phenomenon with NIN's visceral punk ethos applied to mechanical rhythms and arrangements. At the same time, the influence of KMFDM' \"aggro\" style was less obvious but no less ubiquitous, with most bands trying different variations on the idea of fusing heavy-metal guitars and…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":255,"text":"…to a heavier and more frantic sound. New York's Sister Machine Gun (1), the project of keyboardist Chris Randall, offered a more melodic version of KMFDM on Torture Technique (1994). Around the country, Nine Inch Nails and KMFDM imitators included: Los Angeles' Ethyl Meatplow , with Happy Days, Sweetheart (1993), Chicago's Electric Hellfire Club (1), with a classic of…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Early Industrial Group","body":"KMFDM (identified as \"Knights of Ev in Front II IV II\" in the transcript) was mentioned as an example of an early industrial music group, known for its heavy, angry, and aggressive sound that thrived in dark clubs. \"Groups said names like Throbbing Gristle, Cabery Voltaire, Knights of Ev in Front II IV II.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 7: The Other Genres","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amHre9ZZFkU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"German Origin","body":"KMFDM originated from Germany, aligning them with the country often cited as the birthplace of much early electronic and industrial music experimentation. \"KMFDM came out of Germany.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Post-Punk Explosion Part 3: Industrial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zSFhhEaiYwE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Industrial Hip Hop Dabbling","body":"KMFDM is cited as an artist who explored elements of Industrial Hip Hop, especially through beat-heavy keyboard and drum machine music originating in the mid-1980s. \"Ministry came at DM and 9-inch nails dabbled in this, especially with various 12-inch remixes.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 3: The New Genres","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tdTs-4Irv8c"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Sampling of Amen Break","body":"KMFDM is mentioned as one of the artists who have employed the \"Amen Break\" sample in their music. \"And it's been employed by such artists as Slipknot, Primal Scream, Oasis, Nightingale, KMFDM and Literary Thousands more.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Unsung Heroes of Music: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VnXBJqKwkrw"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Sampling of Amen Break","body":"Slipknot is mentioned as one of the artists who have employed the \"Amen Break\" sample in their music. \"And it's been employed by such artists as Slipknot, Primal Scream, Oasis, Nightingale, KMFDM and Literary Thousands more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Slipknot","from_id":32110921912543,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Unsung Heroes of Music: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VnXBJqKwkrw"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Sampling of Amen Break","body":"Primal Scream is mentioned as one of the artists who have employed the \"Amen Break\" sample in their music. \"And it's been employed by such artists as Slipknot, Primal Scream, Oasis, Nightingale, KMFDM and Literary Thousands more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Primal Scream","from_id":241876596213446,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Unsung Heroes of Music: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VnXBJqKwkrw"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Sampling of Amen Break","body":"Oasis is mentioned as one of the artists who have employed the \"Amen Break\" sample in their music. \"And it's been employed by such artists as Slipknot, Primal Scream, Oasis, Nightingale, KMFDM and Literary Thousands more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Oasis","from_id":21712155454134,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Unsung Heroes of Music: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VnXBJqKwkrw"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Sampling of Amen Break","body":"Nightingale is mentioned as one of the artists who have employed the \"Amen Break\" sample in their music. \"And it's been employed by such artists as Slipknot, Primal Scream, Oasis, Nightingale, KMFDM and Literary Thousands more.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Nightingale","from_id":122745005732492,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Unsung Heroes of Music: Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VnXBJqKwkrw"}]}],"charts":[{"id":116548195064561,"type":"album","name":"Opium","list_id":235879004384475,"list":"RYM Top — Electronic — Electro-Industrial","src":"musthear","rank":191,"year":1984,"note":null,"yt":"3_6JDQCZms4","scaruffi":null},{"id":204594879857940,"type":"album","name":"Naive","list_id":224896751673336,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Industrial Rock","src":"musthear","rank":138,"year":1990,"note":null,"yt":"8Dzs4TS_rKc","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":204594879857940,"type":"album","name":"Naive","work_year":1990,"list_id":130183204